{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Sunken Weaving","logline":"When cartographer Veya uncovers a lost archive proving the skybridges were once underwater roads, she must share the truth about the failing bridge network before the Drift Cartel's toll-master Kael buries it and seizes the last stable routes.","theme":"Truths are safer shared than hoarded","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Fading Lines","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_fading_charts","title":"Fading Charts","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya charts skybridges that shift and fray, and finds an anomaly in the oldest survey records: bridge anchor points that match no known sky route and instead trace patterns like seabed roads.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to chart a safe route through the breaking skybridge network and test her late mentor's theory that the isles are drifting apart.","conflict":"The academy's charts disagree with her wind-sight readings, and her stubborn refusal to admit her mentor's method might be incomplete leads her to dismiss the anomaly at first.","outcome":"Veya follows a marginal note in her mentor's papers toward a sealed lower stack, and decides to keep the discovery to herself until she can prove it."},{"id":"scn_sealed_archive","title":"The Sealed Archive","summary":"Beneath Silverspine's lowest stacks, below the cloud layer, Veya breaks into a lost archive and finds weathered maps showing the skybridges as roads laid across a drowned sea floor, with salt-crusted records of the original weaving.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to read the archive and confirm what the anomaly in the charts means.","conflict":"The records are fragile and incomplete, and they contradict everything the Bridge Wardens teach about the First Weaving, so she cannot easily tell whether they are genuine.","outcome":"She copies the key map and learns the bridges' failure follows an old pattern, but she needs someone who knows the cloudstone craft to verify the history.","depends_on":["scn_fading_charts"]},{"id":"scn_kael_tolls","title":"Kael Raises the Toll","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael announces higher skybridge tolls, citing the collapsing network, and hears from a spy that Veya has been seen entering a sealed Silverspine archive.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to secure the Cartel's monopoly on the last stable skybridge routes before the bridges collapse.","conflict":"Merchants and Wardens protest the tolls as part of the Toll War, and Kael's pragmatism clashes with his admiration for Veya's skill, which makes him wary of what she has found.","outcome":"Kael resolves to obtain Veya's charts and sends word to meet her, setting the Cartel against her work.","depends_on":["scn_sealed_archive"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Against the Current","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_proof","title":"Proof at the Forge","summary":"Veya travels to Emberroost, where Bridge Wardens braid cloudstone cables, and shows her copied map to a warden who recognises that the oldest cable weave matches drowned-road paving patterns.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to verify the archive's history by comparing it against the original cloudstone weave.","conflict":"The forge's rule forbids open flame outside shielded pits, and the Wardens distrust any claim that the First Weaving was anything but sky-born; Veya's inability to concede her mentor's theory was only partly right sours the exchange.","outcome":"The weave confirms the archive is genuine, but Veya learns the oldest bridges are failing first, raising the stakes and the pressure to publish.","depends_on":["scn_sealed_archive"]},{"id":"scn_the_offer","title":"Kael's Offer","summary":"Kael meets Veya at Mistral Docks and offers her Cartel patronage and passage fees waived in exchange for exclusive rights to her charts. She refuses to hand them over.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants Veya's charts for the Cartel, while Veya wants to learn how much Kael already knows.","conflict":"Their old apprenticeship bond pulls at both of them; Veya fears becoming like the ambitious cartel leaders, and Kael cannot let her succeed independently.","outcome":"Veya leaves without giving up the charts, and Kael quietly ensures her wind-debt for the crossing is called due early, to pressure her.","depends_on":["scn_kael_tolls","scn_emberroost_proof"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_refuge","title":"Grain and Secrets","summary":"Pressed by the early wind-debt and watched by Cartel enforcers, Veya flees to The Hollow, where she meets Maris, who hides her in a granary and shows her the secret service corridors in exchange for knowledge of wind currents.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants a hidden route and shelter; Maris wants to keep The Hollow fed despite the grain levy.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya will draw the Cartel down on her smuggling routes, while Veya hides the full truth of her archive.","outcome":"They strike an alliance: Veya trades wind-current knowledge for Maris's secret paths, and Maris learns the bridges are failing faster than anyone has admitted.","depends_on":["scn_the_offer"]},{"id":"scn_smuggling_run","title":"The Smuggling Run","summary":"Using Maris's corridors and Veya's wind-sight, the two carry grain across failing skybridges toward the Hollow's stranded neighbours, testing Veya's new safe route.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Maris wants to smuggle enough grain to keep The Hollow fed, and Veya wants to prove her route works.","conflict":"A bridge span shifts unexpectedly because Veya refuses to admit her reading was wrong, and Cartel enforcers close in on Maris's route.","outcome":"They survive and the route works, but the run is spotted and Maris is forced to choose between her isle and her new friendship, as Kael learns of the route.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_refuge"]},{"id":"scn_kael_closes_in","title":"The Ledger Closes","summary":"Kael uses his ledger-mastery to find the weak point in the alliance: Maris's smuggling debts. He seizes Hollow grain barges and moves to lock the remaining stable routes under Cartel control.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to seize the last stable skybridge routes and force Veya to surrender her charts.","conflict":"Maris resists, and Kael's habit of equating price with worth causes him to underestimate her loyalty, while the Wardens accuse him of sabotaging forge-island supplies.","outcome":"Maris is cornered and sends word to Veya, while Kael announces that a toll-gate closure will take effect at the next crossing, leaving a short window.","depends_on":["scn_smuggling_run"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_truth","title":"The Hard Truth","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine and confronts the academy council with the archive, but admits to herself that her mentor's theory of isles drifting apart is wrong: the bridges are failing because the old sea-road structure was never meant to hold in the sky.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the council to accept the archive as proof and open the charts to everyone.","conflict":"The council fears panic and the Cartel's reprisal, and Veya's pride in her mentor's theory makes her argue badly until Maris shows her the wind-debt records as evidence.","outcome":"Veya admits she was wrong, which gives her the real explanation, and she decides to share the charts publicly rather than hoard them, setting up a confrontation with Kael.","depends_on":["scn_kael_closes_in","scn_emberroost_proof"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Crossing","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_forge_standoff","title":"Standoff at the Forge","summary":"Kael arrives at Emberroost with Cartel enforcers to seize the Wardens' cables and Veya's charts, just as Veya and Maris bring the copied archive maps. Veya publicly reveals that the bridges were once underwater roads and are failing because they are fatigued.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to share the truth and a safe route with everyone, while Kael wants the charts and the last stable routes.","conflict":"A confrontation between rivals: Kael's control against Veya's openness, with the shielded forge-pits and no-flame rule making any rash move risk severing a bridge.","outcome":"Kael sees that the data proves the routes cannot be held by anyone, but he cannot yet let go, and a cable begins to fail under the strain.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_truth"]},{"id":"scn_bridge_gambit","title":"The Breaking Span","summary":"With a skybridge failing and merchants stranded on it, Veya uses wind-sight to guide a crossing, Maris leads people through service corridors, and Kael must decide whether to hold the toll-gates closed or open them.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to chart a safe route out of the breaking network; Kael wants to keep control of the routes.","conflict":"Closing the gates would trap travellers, but opening them breaks the Cartel's monopoly, forcing Kael to weigh price against worth.","outcome":"Kael opens the gates and lets Veya's route be used, the stranded travellers are saved, and the Cartel's grip on the routes breaks.","depends_on":["scn_forge_standoff"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What the Weaving Remembers","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_new_charts","title":"Charts for Everyone","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya publishes the shared charts and the archive's history, and Wardens, millers and merchants begin planning repairs together, while she owns her mistake about her mentor's theory.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the charts shared so the network can be repaired and travellers kept safe.","conflict":"Some Wardens resist the history that the bridges were once underwater roads, and Veya must accept credit shared rather than claimed.","outcome":"The charts are openly distributed and a joint repair effort begins, and Veya's arc of sharing truth is complete.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_gambit"]},{"id":"scn_kael_ledger","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael faces the Cartel's anger and tallies what control has cost him, then agrees to repay wind-debt in labour to the repair effort and drops the grain levy on The Hollow.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to preserve what he can of the Cartel's standing without the monopoly.","conflict":"The Cartel's princes demand he reverse the decision, and his pride resists admitting that control cost more than it gained.","outcome":"Kael accepts a reduced, accountable role, repaying his debts through labour, and his rivalry with Veya turns into wary respect.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_gambit","scn_new_charts"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Harvest Under Open Sky","summary":"In The Hollow, windmills turn again as grain moves freely along the new routes, and Maris, no longer needing to hide her paths, decides which of them to share.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants to see The Hollow fed and secure without smuggling.","conflict":"Her slow trust and reluctance to forgive make her hesitate to reveal her corridors, even to a friend.","outcome":"Maris accepts that hiding was brave but standing openly is braver, shares her paths with Veya and the Hollow Circle, and the isles begin to settle into a new rhythm.","depends_on":["scn_kael_ledger"]}]}]}
</Output>
