.","outcome":"They survive and the route works, but the run is spotted and Maris is forced to choose between her isle and her new friendship, as Kael learns of the route.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_refuge"]},{"id":"scn_kael_closes_in","title":"The Ledger Closes","summary":"Kael uses his ledger-mastery to find the weak point in the alliance: Maris's smuggling debts. He seizes Hollow grain barges and moves to lock the remaining stable routes under Cartel control.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to seize the last stable skybridge routes and force Veya to surrender her charts.","conflict":"Maris resists, and Kael's habit of equating price with worth causes him to underestimate her loyalty, while the Wardens accuse him of sabotaging forge-island supplies.","outcome":"Maris is cornered and sends word to Veya, while Kael announces that a toll-gate closure will take effect at the next crossing, leaving a short window.","depends_on":["scn_smuggling_run"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_truth","title":"The Hard Truth","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine and confronts the academy council with the archive, but admits to herself that her mentor's theory of isles drifting apart is wrong: the bridges are failing because the old sea-road structure was never meant to hold in the sky.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the council to accept the archive as proof and open the charts to everyone.","conflict":"The council fears panic and the Cartel's reprisal, and Veya's pride in her mentor's theory makes her argue badly until Maris shows her the wind-debt records as evidence.","outcome":"Veya admits she was wrong, which gives her the real explanation, and she decides to share the charts publicly rather than hoard them, setting up a confrontation with Kael.","depends_on":["scn_kael_closes_in","scn_emberroost_proof"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Crossing","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_forge_standoff","title":"Standoff at the Forge","summary":"Kael arrives at Emberroost with Cartel enforcers to seize the Wardens' cables and Veya's charts, just as Veya and Maris bring the copied archive maps. Veya publicly reveals that the bridges were once underwater roads and are failing because they are fatigued.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to share the truth and a safe route with everyone, while Kael wants the charts and the last stable routes.","conflict":"A confrontation between rivals: Kael's control against Veya's openness, with the shielded forge-pits and no-flame rule making any rash move risk severing a bridge.","outcome":"Kael sees that the data proves the routes cannot be held by anyone, but he cannot yet let go, and a cable begins to fail under the strain.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_truth"]},{"id":"scn_bridge_gambit","title":"The Breaking Span","summary":"With a skybridge failing and merchants stranded on it, Veya uses wind-sight to guide a crossing, Maris leads people through service corridors, and Kael must decide whether to hold the toll-gates closed or open them.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to chart a safe route out of the breaking network; Kael wants to keep control of the routes.","conflict":"Closing the gates would trap travellers, but opening them breaks the Cartel's monopoly, forcing Kael to weigh price against worth.","outcome":"Kael opens the gates and lets Veya's route be used, the stranded travellers are saved, and the Cartel's grip on the routes breaks.","depends_on":["scn_forge_standoff"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What the Weaving Remembers","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_new_charts","title":"Charts for Everyone","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya publishes the shared charts and the archive's history, and Wardens, millers and merchants begin planning repairs together, while she owns her mistake about her mentor's theory.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the charts shared so the network can be repaired and travellers kept safe.","conflict":"Some Wardens resist the history that the bridges were once underwater roads, and Veya must accept credit shared rather than claimed.","outcome":"The charts are openly distributed and a joint repair effort begins, and Veya's arc of sharing truth is complete.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_gambit"]},{"id":"scn_kael_ledger","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael faces the Cartel's anger and tallies what control has cost him, then agrees to repay wind-debt in labour to the repair effort and drops the grain levy on The Hollow.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to preserve what he can of the Cartel's standing without the monopoly.","conflict":"The Cartel's princes demand he reverse the decision, and his pride resists admitting that control cost more than it gained.","outcome":"Kael accepts a reduced, accountable role, repaying his debts through labour, and his rivalry with Veya turns into wary respect.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_gambit","scn_new_charts"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Harvest Under Open Sky","summary":"In The Hollow, windmills turn again as grain moves freely along the new routes, and Maris, no longer needing to hide her paths, decides which of them to share.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants to see The Hollow fed and secure without smuggling.","conflict":"Her slow trust and reluctance to forgive make her hesitate to reveal her corridors, even to a friend.","outcome":"Maris accepts that hiding was brave but standing openly is braver, shares her paths with Veya and the Hollow Circle, and the isles begin to settle into a new rhythm.","depends_on":["scn_kael_ledger"]}]}]}
