":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_forge_standoff","title":"Standoff at the Forge","summary":"Kael arrives at Emberroost with Cartel enforcers to seize the Wardens' cables and Veya's charts, just as Veya and Maris bring the copied archive maps. Veya publicly reveals that the bridges were once underwater roads and are failing because they are fatigued.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to share the truth and a safe route with everyone, while Kael wants the charts and the last stable routes.","conflict":"A confrontation between rivals: Kael's control against Veya's openness, with the shielded forge-pits and no-flame rule making any rash move risk severing a bridge.","outcome":"Kael sees that the data proves the routes cannot be held by anyone, but he cannot yet let go, and a cable begins to fail under the strain.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_truth"]},{"id":"scn_bridge_gambit","title":"The Breaking Span","summary":"With a skybridge failing and merchants stranded on it, Veya uses wind-sight to guide a crossing, Maris leads people through service corridors, and Kael must decide whether to hold the toll-gates closed or open them.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to chart a safe route out of the breaking network; Kael wants to keep control of the routes.","conflict":"Closing the gates would trap travellers, but opening them breaks the Cartel's monopoly, forcing Kael to weigh price against worth.","outcome":"Kael opens the gates and lets Veya's route be used, the stranded travellers are saved, and the Cartel's grip on the routes breaks.","depends_on":["scn_forge_standoff"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What the Weaving Remembers","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_new_charts","title":"Charts for Everyone","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya publishes the shared charts and the archive's history, and Wardens, millers and merchant