"scn_grain_whisper","title":"Grain and Whispers","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris moves smuggled grain past Cartel enforcers. She notices that the sleepers' calm is spreading to her isle, and that her silo corridors no longer match her memory.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Maris wants to smuggle enough grain to feed The Hollow through the levy.","conflict":"Enforcers tighten around her routes, and the changed corridors cost her time she does not have.","outcome":"Maris decides to carry word of the shifting paths to Veya, since only a cartographer could make sense of them.","depends_on":["scn_stalled_crossing"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"The Dreaming Map","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_alliance_of_paths","title":"A Trade of Paths","summary":"Maris finds Veya and the two trade knowledge. Maris offers her service corridors, and Veya offers her reading of the wind. Together they see that the new corridors match the new bridges on the charts.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to confirm that the changes to the map are real, and Maris wants a way to protect her isle.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya of working for the Cartel. Veya hoards her unfinished theory rather than sharing it.","outcome":"They agree to go to the skybridge together. Veya keeps back her fear that the map is being rewritten by the sleepers.","depends_on":["scn_charts_shift","scn_grain_whisper"]},{"id":"scn_kael_offer","title":"The Toll-Master's Offer","summary":"Kael meets Veya at Mistral Docks and offers to fund her survey in exchange for exclusive rights to the charts. He admires her skill and needs her routes.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to seize control of the new routes by securing her charts. Veya wants access to the sealed span.","conflict":"Veya will not let him control the charts, but she needs his permission to reach the span. Kael cannot let her succeed without him.","outcome":"Veya refuses the exclusive deal and Kael grants her limited access under Cartel watch, intending to take the charts afterward.","depends_on":["scn_alliance_of_paths"]},{"id":"scn_sleepers_dream","title":"Among the Sleepers","summary":"On the skybridge, Veya and Maris find the merchants sleeping side by side. The span's cables shift in step with their breathing. Veya's wind-sight shows that the bridge moves when the sleepers dream. Maris finds a service passage on a span that is not on any chart.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to learn how the dreams change the map. Kael wants to know what she finds.","conflict":"Kael's watchers press them for results. Veya's refusal to admit that her mentor's theory may be incomplete leads her to chart a bridge that vanishes under her feet.","outcome":"Maris pulls Veya back from the failing span. Veya admits the danger to Maris but not to Kael, who learns enough to begin moving ahead of them.","depends_on":["scn_kael_offer"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_cables","title":"Cables at Emberroost","summary":"Veya and Maris take the sleepers' map to the Bridge Wardens at Emberroost. The Wardens suspect Kael of sabotaging forge supplies, and the cable stocks they need to anchor the bridges are short. A stray spark from a careless forge worker nearly severs a cable in the aftermath.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the Wardens to help her anchor a safe route. Maris wants to find passages that keep her isle supplied.","conflict":"The Wardens will not share their stock with someone who works with the Cartel's grain smugglers. Maris's old grudges flare when she is questioned.","outcome":"Veya shares her whole theory openly, for the first time, to win the Wardens' trust. They agree to lend cables if she can reach the stable span before Kael does.","depends_on":["scn_sleepers_dream"]},{"id":"scn_kael_seizes","title":"The Last Stable Routes","summary":"Kael uses Veya's partial charts to close the last stable skybridge routes to non-Cartel traffic. Maris's smuggling lines are cut and The Hollow is isolated.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to lock down the surviving routes before the bridges fail. Maris wants to get grain through.","conflict":"Kael's enforcers corner Maris. His ledger-mastery finds her weakest point: her loyalty to her home.","outcome":"Maris is forced to choose, and she breaks her silence to send word to Veya that the routes are closed. Kael learns that the sleepers are still reshaping the span.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_cables"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Waking","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_span_confrontation","title":"Confrontation on the Span","summary":"Veya, Maris and the Wardens' cables meet Kael on the sleepers' skybridge as it begins to unravel. Veya charts the one route the dreams have left stable and refuses to give it to Kael alone. Kael demands it at any cost.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to chart and share a safe route out. Kael wants to seize the last stable route.","conflict":"The span shifts underfoot, and Kael's price-for-everything instinct clashes with Veya's refusal to hoard. Maris must choose between hiding and standing with Veya.","outcome":"Kael tries to take the chart by force and the span begins to fail, leaving him stranded on a collapsing section.","depends_on":["scn_kael_seizes"]},{"id":"scn_the_choice","title":"What Control Costs","summary":"With Kael cut off, Veya must admit that her chart is incomplete and needs Kael's knowledge of the traders' weakest links to finish. Maris leads them through the uncharted service passage. Kael sees that holding the route alone would doom the sleepers.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to save everyone on the span. Kael wants to survive and keep his monopoly.","conflict":"Veya's flaw means admitting she was wrong. Kael's belief that price equals worth is challenged by the sleepers' lives.","outcome":"Kael yields the route to shared use. The group crosses through Maris's passage and the sleepers are carried to safety, waking as the calm breaks.","depends_on":["scn_span_confrontation"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"After the Calm","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_charts_shared","title":"Charts Shared","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya publishes the full chart to all factions, including her own mistakes. The Academy and the Wardens begin anchoring the safe routes. The merchants wake with no memory of the dreams, but the map remains changed.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to make the chart public so no single faction can hoard it.","conflict":"Some Academy scholars say publishing will empower the Cartel, and her old wish for recognition tempts her to claim sole credit.","outcome":"Veya credits Maris and the Wardens and releases the charts openly, accepting the cost to her reputation.","depends_on":["scn_the_choice"]},{"id":"scn_kael_ledger","title":"Kael's Reckoning","summary":"Kael faces the Cartel's council, which blames him for the stall and the lost tolls. He discovers that control cost him more than it gained, and he opens the surviving routes under a reduced toll.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to salvage the Cartel's standing and his own place within it.","conflict":"The Cartel council wants him to hold the monopoly, and Veya's open charts have removed his leverage.","outcome":"Kael accepts a lower toll and a shared route in exchange for survival, and Veya acknowledges his help on the span.","depends_on":["scn_charts_shared"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_fed","title":"The Hollow Fed","summary":"With routes reopened, Maris brings grain to The Hollow openly. She accepts that hiding was brave but that standing in the open is possible now. The isle's calm is ordinary again, though its corridors remain changed.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants The Hollow fed and her smuggling to end safely.","conflict":"Maris's slow trust is tested by the Hollow Circle's doubts about Cartel promises, and by her own wariness of Veya.","outcome":"Veya and Maris part as friends, and Maris keeps the unmapped corridors as the isle's quiet inheritance.","depends_on":["scn_kael_ledger"]}]}]}
