{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Cartographer's Mark","logline":"When the skybridges of Aetheria begin to fail, cartographer Veya must chart a safe route and share her findings before the Drift Cartel's toll-master Kael seizes the last stable routes and buries her charts, leaving the isles to drift apart.","theme":"Truth shared is safer than truth hoarded","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"Fading Bridges","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_charts","title":"The Fading Charts","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya uses her wind-sight to read the currents and discovers that several skybridges are weakening faster than her late mentor predicted. An old academy keeper recites a prophecy that a chosen one will repair the bridges, and Veya dismisses it as superstition.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Confirm that the skybridge network is breaking by charting the shifting currents.","conflict":"Her readings contradict the Academy's official charts, and her stubborn refusal to doubt her own conclusions leaves her isolated from the scholars who might help.","outcome":"Veya completes a draft chart showing a single stable route and resolves to protect it, though she tells no one beyond the Wardens."},{"id":"scn_mistral_ledger","title":"Toll at Mistral Docks","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael studies the Cartel's ledgers and learns that Wardens are surveying the failing bridges. He recognises that whoever holds the last stable routes will control all trade after the collapse, and he sets out to seize them.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Identify which skybridge routes will remain stable so the Cartel can claim them.","conflict":"The Cartel's own maps are outdated, and the Bridge Wardens accuse him of sabotaging forge-island supplies, which draws scrutiny to his methods.","outcome":"Kael learns that Veya's new charts hold the answer and decides he must obtain them, whatever the cost.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_charts"]},{"id":"scn_dock_meeting","title":"Old Apprentices","summary":"Veya travels to Mistral Docks to pay the wind-debt her crossing has accrued and to find a pilot. Kael greets her warmly and offers to buy her charts, reminding her they were apprentices together. She refuses, and he lets her go with a veiled warning.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to settle her wind-debt and secure passage without revealing her charts; Kael wants to acquire them.","conflict":"Kael's charm and his offer of recognition play on Veya's wish to be acknowledged, while she fears becoming like the Cartel leaders.","outcome":"Veya refuses to sell, making Kael her open rival, and she realises she can no longer trust the docks and needs allies.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_charts","scn_mistral_ledger"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Breaking Routes","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_refuge","title":"Grain and Secrets","summary":"Veya follows the grain trade to The Hollow, where Maris is hiding smuggled grain from the Cartel levy. Maris distrusts her at first, but the two trade wind-current knowledge for Maris's unmapped service corridors.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya seeks a hidden path off the Cartel-watched lanes; Maris seeks to keep her isle fed through the crisis.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya's charts will draw Cartel attention to the Hollow, while Veya's stubbornness makes her reluctant to share her findings.","outcome":"They form an alliance, and Maris agrees to guide Veya through the corridors in exchange for Veya's help reading safe wind windows for the smuggling runs.","depends_on":["scn_dock_meeting"]},{"id":"scn_enforcers_closing","title":"Cartel Enforcers","summary":"Cartel enforcers sent by Kael track the smuggling routes to the Hollow's windmills. Maris uses her pathfinding to lead them through the service corridors while Veya reads the wind to time their escape.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Escape the enforcers with the charts and the grain intact; Kael wants the charts seized.","conflict":"Veya insists on her own timing even when Maris warns the wind has shifted, and the error costs them part of the grain stores.","outcome":"They escape with the charts but lose grain, and Maris bitterly questions whether Veya's pride will cost her isle more.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_refuge"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_forge","title":"Cables of Cloudstone","summary":"Veya and Maris reach Emberroost, where the Bridge Wardens braid cloudstone cables. Veya shows them her chart of the one stable route, and the Wardens confirm the weakening is real. The prophecy is whispered among the forge workers, who hope Veya is the chosen one.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Persuade the Wardens to use the chart to reinforce the stable route before it fails.","conflict":"The Wardens lack cloudstone because Cartel interference has cut their supplies, and Veya must admit her chart is incomplete, which is hard for her to do.","outcome":"Veya admits the gap and agrees to complete the chart with the Wardens, who promise to reinforce the route if she can reach the last unmapped span.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_closing"]},{"id":"scn_kael_sabotage","title":"The Severed Cable","summary":"Kael arrives at Emberroost under a trade truce and offers the Wardens protected supplies in return for Veya's charts. When she refuses, a spark from a Cartel lantern, carried against the ban on open flame aloft, severs a cable and a section of bridge drops away.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to force Veya to hand over the charts; Veya wants to stop the Cartel from controlling the bridges.","conflict":"Kael's internal conflict surfaces as he admires Veya yet pressures her, and the accident he caused shows control costing more than it gains.","outcome":"The stable route is cut short, Kael is shaken and withdraws, and Veya realises the only way forward is to chart the remaining span and share it openly.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_forge"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Span","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_reveal","title":"The Open Chart","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine Academy with Maris and completes the chart of the last span, then decides to copy it for every isle rather than hoard it. Kael arrives to seize it, and the confrontation plays out before the assembled cartographers.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to publish the full chart so all isles can use the stable route; Kael wants to seize the last stable routes for the Cartel.","conflict":"Kael argues that trade must be regulated and offers Veya fame in return for silence, testing her fear of becoming like him, while Veya's old habit of hoarding truth tempts her to refuse to share.","outcome":"Veya shares the chart openly, and Kael, seeing the collapse he caused and the worth of what she gives away, relinquishes his claim and orders the Cartel to stand down.","depends_on":["scn_kael_sabotage"]},{"id":"scn_last_crossing","title":"Crossing the Last Span","summary":"With the chart public, Veya, Kael and Maris cross the failing span to anchor the Wardens' reinforcement cables. Veya's wind-sight guides them, Maris's pathfinding finds the footing, and Kael's ledger-mastery spots the weak point in the cables. The prophecy of a chosen one is fulfilled by many hands.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Anchor the reinforcement cables before the final stable route collapses.","conflict":"Veya must accept Kael's reading of the cable weakness over her own, and Maris must trust Kael enough to follow him onto the span.","outcome":"The cables hold and the route is saved, and the three prove that shared knowledge repairs what hoarded knowledge could not.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_reveal"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"Shared Skies","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_mistral_accord","title":"The Docks Accord","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael presents the Cartel with a new accord that lowers tolls on the saved route, accepting that control costs more than it gains. The Wardens receive cloudstone supplies, and Veya's wind-debt is formally settled.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to convince the Cartel to accept shared use of the route; Veya wants the toll war ended.","conflict":"Cartel princes resist losing their monopoly, and Kael must spend his own influence to win them over.","outcome":"The accord passes, ending the Toll War, and Kael loses some power but gains an honest rival in Veya.","depends_on":["scn_last_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Harvest Without Levy","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris welcomes grain shipments along the saved route now that the levy has been eased by the accord. She finds that hiding was brave but that standing in the open is also possible, and she forgives Veya.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants the Hollow fed without smuggling; Veya wants to repair the friendship strained by her pride.","conflict":"Maris's reluctance to forgive meets Veya's difficulty admitting fault, and each must yield to the other.","outcome":"Veya admits she was wrong about the wind window, Maris forgives her, and The Hollow's grain flows openly across the archipelago.","depends_on":["scn_mistral_accord"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_new_charts","title":"A Shared Map","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya adds her late mentor's name to the new chart and opens the Academy's doors to cartographers from every isle, as the archipelago's drift continues but now charted by all.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to honour her mentor's theory and establish a shared chart of the drifting isles.","conflict":"Some scholars cling to the old official charts, and Veya must accept their critique rather than dismiss it.","outcome":"The Academy adopts the shared charting method, and Veya's mark on the map becomes a symbol of knowledge given freely.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_harvest"]}]}]}
