ternal conflict surfaces as he admires Veya yet pressures her, and the accident he caused shows control costing more than it gains.","outcome":"The stable route is cut short, Kael is shaken and withdraws, and Veya realises the only way forward is to chart the remaining span and share it openly.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_forge"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Span","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_reveal","title":"The Open Chart","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine Academy with Maris and completes the chart of the last span, then decides to copy it for every isle rather than hoard it. Kael arrives to seize it, and the confrontation plays out before the assembled cartographers.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to publish the full chart so all isles can use the stable route; Kael wants to seize the last stable routes for the Cartel.","conflict":"Kael argues that trade must be regulated and offers Veya fame in return for silence, testing her fear of becoming like him, while Veya's old habit of hoarding truth tempts her to refuse to share.","outcome":"Veya shares the chart openly, and Kael, seeing the collapse he caused and the worth of what she gives away, relinquishes his claim and orders the Cartel to stand down.","depends_on":["scn_kael_sabotage"]},{"id":"scn_last_crossing","title":"Crossing the Last Span","summary":"With the chart public, Veya, Kael and Maris cross the failing span to anchor the Wardens' reinforcement cables. Veya's wind-sight guides them, Maris's pathfinding finds the footing, and Kael's ledger-mastery spots the weak point in the cables. The prophecy of a chosen one is fulfilled by many hands.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Anchor the reinforcement cables before the final stable route collapses.","conflict":"Veya must accept Kael's reading of the cable weakness over her own, and Maris must trust Kael enough to follow him onto the span.","outcome":"The cables hold and the route is saved, and the three prove that shared knowledge repairs what hoarded knowledge could not.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_reveal"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"Shared Skies","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_mistral_accord","title":"The Docks Accord","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael presents the Cartel with a new accord that lowers tolls on the saved route, accepting that control costs more than it gains. The Wardens receive cloudstone supplies, and Veya's wind-debt is formally settled.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to convince the Cartel to accept shared use of the route; Veya wants the toll war ended.","conflict":"Cartel princes resist losing their monopoly, and Kael must spend his own influence to win them over.","outcome":"The accord passes, ending the Toll War, and Kael loses some power but gains an honest rival in Veya.","depends_on":["scn_last_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Harvest Without Levy","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris welcomes grain shipments along the saved route now that the levy has been eased by the accord. She finds that hiding was brave but that standing in the open is also possible, and she forgives Veya.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants the Hollow fed without smuggling; Veya wants to repair the friendship strained by her pride.","conflict":"Maris's reluctance to forgive meets Veya's difficulty admitting fault, and each must yield to the other.","outcome":"Veya admits she was wrong about the wind window, Maris forgives her, and The Hollow's grain flows openly across the archipelago.","depends_on":["scn_mistral_accord"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_new_charts","title":"A Shared Map","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya adds her late mentor's name to the new chart and opens the Academy's doors 